WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.042 --> 00:00:02.920
Paul:
Are you just gonna burn down
your career and take me with you?

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:03.420
Coin-flip?

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:03.629
Ahh!

00:00:03.629 --> 00:00:04.213
(Crash)

00:00:04.213 --> 00:00:05.005
Get out of here.

00:00:08.133 --> 00:00:09.426
What's on your mind today?

00:00:09.426 --> 00:00:14.431
Like I want to change, but I’m
not particularly open to make
those changes.

00:00:14.431 --> 00:00:15.098
I'm trying.

00:00:15.098 --> 00:00:19.519
Every time I get rid of one
compulsion, another compulsion
comes up.

00:00:20.187 --> 00:00:21.271
Are you yawning right now?

00:00:21.271 --> 00:00:23.732
Spoiler alert, I feel like I'm
stuck.

00:00:27.236 --> 00:00:29.404
Right, how does that make you
feel?

00:00:29.404 --> 00:00:31.031
(People screaming)

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:32.157
(Splash)

00:00:32.991 --> 00:00:33.659
Jimmy.

00:00:33.659 --> 00:00:34.826
Liz, hey.

00:00:34.826 --> 00:00:36.537
It's three in the morning. 

00:00:36.537 --> 00:00:37.287
I'm sorry.

00:00:37.287 --> 00:00:38.247
What's in that bowl?

00:00:38.247 --> 00:00:38.830
Pretzels.

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:39.915
The other bowl?

00:00:39.915 --> 00:00:41.041
Maybe some painkillers.

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:41.750
Maybe?

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.126
There's painkiller in there,
yeah.

00:00:43.585 --> 00:00:46.546
Liz:
I have to ask, is this you
forever?

00:00:47.172 --> 00:00:48.173
Jimmy:
I don’t know.

00:00:49.174 --> 00:00:53.053
♪Crush a bit, little bit, roll
it up, take a hit.♪

00:00:54.096 --> 00:00:55.138
Jimmy:
Oh, hey,

00:00:55.138 --> 00:00:55.764
Paul.

00:00:56.098 --> 00:00:57.266
I’m worried about you, kid.

00:00:57.766 --> 00:00:58.850
Jimmy:
I’ve been grieving her.

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:00.060
(Crying)

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.228
Paul:
You’ve been numbing.

00:01:01.228 --> 00:01:02.437
Ahh!
(Crash)

00:01:02.479 --> 00:01:04.064
Stop, you’re doing sad face.

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:05.148
This is just face.

00:01:05.816 --> 00:01:07.192
I have resting dead wife face.

00:01:07.192 --> 00:01:08.151
(Laughing)

00:01:08.151 --> 00:01:13.282
He just kept going on and on
about how dumb I am, but he
loves me.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.243
Your husband is emotionally
abusive.

00:01:16.243 --> 00:01:20.455
He’s not working on it. He
doesn’t intend to. Just leave
him.

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:22.499
Okay.

00:01:23.834 --> 00:01:25.877
♪I'm on the pursuit of
happiness.♪

00:01:25.877 --> 00:01:28.714
I think I can help people
if I get my hands a little bit
dirtier.

00:01:29.047 --> 00:01:30.799
Your mom wanted you to scatter
her ashes, right?

00:01:30.799 --> 00:01:31.800
Jimmy:
We know what they should do.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:33.343
Don’t you ever want to just
shake them?

00:01:33.343 --> 00:01:34.386
But we don’t shake them.

00:01:34.386 --> 00:01:35.721
Jimmy:
I take that back, run!
-Huh.

00:01:36.305 --> 00:01:37.639
It sounds so unethical.

00:01:37.639 --> 00:01:40.517
Are you just gonna burn down
your career and take me with
you? 

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:42.102
Coin-flip?

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:43.145
Get out of here.

00:01:44.479 --> 00:01:45.772
Wait, this is my office.

00:01:45.856 --> 00:01:47.774
It took you longer than it
should’ve.

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:50.235
My patients are really thriving.

00:01:50.235 --> 00:01:51.862
Jimmy:
This thing I’m doing is really
working.

00:01:51.862 --> 00:01:52.821
Jimmy:
I’m right behind you.

00:01:54.573 --> 00:01:56.158
(Yelling)

00:01:58.410 --> 00:02:01.246
Nobody gets through this life
unscathed.

00:02:01.246 --> 00:02:02.706
I can’t remember Mom’s laugh.

00:02:02.706 --> 00:02:04.624
I can feel her slipping away.

00:02:06.043 --> 00:02:07.336
Paul:
You’re faced with a choice.

00:02:07.336 --> 00:02:09.796
Paul:
Are you going to let your grief
drown you,

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:10.922
or are you going to face it

00:02:10.922 --> 00:02:12.549
Paul:
come out the other side?

00:02:13.508 --> 00:02:14.134
(Cheering)

00:02:15.052 --> 00:02:16.428
It’s nice to see you have your
spark back.

00:02:16.428 --> 00:02:19.389
♪♪

00:02:19.389 --> 00:02:20.515
Sean:
You just going to leave your car
here?

00:02:20.515 --> 00:02:23.894
I’m a white guy in Pasadena, the
cops will probably just take it
back to my house for me.

00:02:24.227 --> 00:02:25.020
Sean:
Must be nice.

00:02:25.228 --> 00:02:29.232
♪I'm on the pursuit of
happiness, and I know.♪

00:02:29.483 --> 00:02:30.275
Derek, how’s it going?

00:02:30.275 --> 00:02:31.860
Just walking the dog I didn’t
want.

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:33.987
My patient moved into her
sister’s start.

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:36.073
Sounds like the day’s off to a
great start for both of us.

